Package: yume
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Suggests:
 tor,
 yume-gui
Description: stealth transport client and server
 YUME tunnels application streams through an authenticated TLS 1.3 carrier
 that can use an HTTP/2 camouflage preface. It provides a client, a server
 daemon, SOCKS mode, local and reverse forwarding, relay features, and
 optional routing through external anonymity networks such as Tor.
 .
 This Debian build links against the system-installed libbasefwx, which
 provides AES, Argon2id, and ML-KEM-768 post-quantum inner crypto.

Package: yume-gui
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!nogui>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 yume (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends:
 libayatana-appindicator3-1
Description: graphical desktop client for the Yume transport
 yume-gui is an optional Dear ImGui-based desktop application that
 embeds the yume_core library directly. It provides client connection
 management, local server hosting, key management (Ed25519 and
 ML-KEM-768), a relay directory and chat, log inspection, and a
 system tray icon with minimise-to-tray behaviour.
 .
 This package is independent of the CLI binaries and can be installed
 alongside them. The CLI continues to be the supported automation
 surface; the GUI is for desktop users.
